# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The dataset is NOT committed.
#
# GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB, and the Roboflow export is
# ~425 MB packed / ~453 MB extracted, so a repository carrying it cannot be
# pushed at all.  Download the YOLO-format export of
#
#     https://universe.roboflow.com/hobby-projs/puzzle-vrkx6-9xh3l/dataset/1
#
# and unpack it into detection/ ; README.md ("Getting the dataset") gives the
# expected layout.
#
# Everything the brief asks to be *submitted* -- source, tests, results,
# figures, the report, and eight sample photographs with their answer keys in
# data/ -- is committed and does not depend on this directory.  main.py falls
# back to data/ automatically when detection/ is absent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
detection/
detection.rar
*.rar
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated intermediates -- regenerated on demand, never deliverables.
#
# results/milestone2/cache/ holds the pickled training puzzles that
# main_milestone2.py rebuilds whenever they are missing.  It is a single file
# of roughly 860 MB, and it was committed once by accident; ignoring it is
# what stops that from happening again.  Note that an ignore rule has no
# effect on a file git is *already* tracking, which is why that one had to be
# removed from the index with `git rm --cached` first.
#
# Deliberately still committed, because the reports cite them: the trained
# checkpoints results/milestone2/*.pt (1.8 MB total) and every JSON under
# results/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cache/
*.pkl
